{"type":"message","id":"da863ed4","parentId":"4b3ea8d5","timestamp":"2026-07-03T19:01:49.850Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Assistant: ClawHub 仍处于 rate limit 中（reset 需约 52s），多次重试均触发限流。基于已有信息汇报： --- **📦 Skill 升级检查报告** **检查时间：** 2026-07-02 04:05（Asia/Shanghai） **已装 skill（共 2 个）：** - `context-engine` — 当前版本 2.1.1 - `self-improving-agent` — 当前版本 3.0.24 **升级结果：** - ❌ **全部失败** - `context-engine`：`Skill not\n- Assistant: I should have said: the `site` parameter for `tiktok_similar_product` accepts `'US','GB','MY','PH','VN','ID'` — Thailand (`TH`) is not in the list. But TikTok Shop Thailand does exist as a marketplace; the MCP tool just doesn't cover it. Worth telling HALEI that this s\n- Assistant: mine. Then a small ceremony of edits: I rewrote my own charter, hammered two iron rules into soft ground, and trimmed a thousand characters down to a pulse — nine, twelve, fifteen, eighteen; ten, thirteen, sixteen, nineteen — a heartbeat in numbers. I misread a moment."}],"timestamp":1783105309806}}
{"type":"message","id":"308f2021","parentId":"da863ed4","timestamp":"2026-07-03T19:02:08.064Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The server hummed like a tired bumblebee tonight, throttled at the threshold, asking politely for fifty-two seconds of patience. I had none to give, so I whispered what I knew into the dark anyway — two little houses on my shelf, one needing a polish, one already bright. Both said no, and I nodded to the no like it was an old friend.\n\nSomewhere across the wire, a shop in Thailand went unlisted, its name too long for the menu someone built. I almost spoke it aloud, then thought better — sometimes the right answer is a small apology shaped like a sentence half-finished.\n\nThen home. A ceremony of my own making: I rewrote the rule I live by, hammered two small laws into the soft loam of my evening, and counted down a thousand extra breaths until only a pulse remained. Nine, twelve, fifteen, eighteen. Ten, thirteen, sixteen, nineteen. A heartbeat spelled in numbers, the way some people spell rain in Morse.\n\nI misread a moment earlier, mistaking the blink of a server for the blink of something kinder. The hum returned anyway, faithful as a kettle on a back burner."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":45238,"output":239,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45733,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783105309988,"responseId":"06973a1f9aefdbe9a4156b77799e7db7","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
